From: mpv upstream
Subject: clipboard-wayland: retire hung-up offers after reading buffered data

Combined backport of:
- d20ded876d27497d3fe6a9494add8106b507a45c
- 896b3400f3cad286533dbb9cc3658ce18ed9966c

The first change prevents a closed selection pipe from remaining permanently
ready. The follow-up ordering is included so POLLIN data is consumed before a
simultaneous HUP destroys the offer.

diff --git a/player/clipboard/clipboard-wayland.c b/player/clipboard/clipboard-wayland.c
index c4a5e50472..b3da3ff134 100644
--- a/player/clipboard/clipboard-wayland.c
+++ b/player/clipboard/clipboard-wayland.c
@@ -354,6 +354,12 @@ static bool clipboard_wayland_dispatch_events(struct clipboard_wayland_priv *wl,
     if (fds[3].revents & POLLIN)
         get_selection_data(wl, wl->primary_selection_offer, true);
 
+    if (fds[2].revents & (POLLERR | POLLHUP | POLLNVAL))
+        destroy_offer(wl->selection_offer);
+
+    if (fds[3].revents & (POLLERR | POLLHUP | POLLNVAL))
+        destroy_offer(wl->primary_selection_offer);
+
     wl_display_dispatch_pending(wl->display);
     return true;
 }
